            <h2>Which sentence uses the verb "to be" in the correct form?</h2>
            <p>The correct answer is:</p>
            <p><strong>c) He is a doctor.</strong></p>
            <p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>
            <p>
                The verb <strong>"to be"</strong> changes depending on the subject:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>I <strong>am</strong></li>
                <li>You <strong>are</strong></li>
                <li>He/She/It <strong>is</strong></li>
                <li>We/You/They <strong>are</strong></li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Therefore, <em>"He is a doctor"</em> is correct because "he" takes "is".
            </p>
